  "description": "Circuit-level design pedagogy for variable-frequency drives (VFDs) that control AC motor speed and torque. Covers the rectifier-to-DC-bus-to-inverter signal chain, V/f scalar control with constant volts-per-hertz ratio, vector/field-oriented control concepts, PWM carrier-frequency tradeoffs, and bearing-current mitigation. Owns the VFD circuit DESIGN; system-level drive packaging and installation belong to power-electronics.",
